Package: BetterGG
Title: APA-Style Additions to 'ggstatsplot'
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Gilad", "Feldman", email = "giladfel@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: An add-on layer for 'ggstatsplot'. Loads after 'ggstatsplot' and
    provides the same plotting functions with APA-style p-values (three
    decimals, no leading zero, "p < .001" below .001). Every p-value is
    re-formatted from the exact value 'ggstatsplot' computed, never from the
    rounded text shown on the plot.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
Depends:
    R (>= 4.5.0),
    ggstatsplot (>= 1.1.3)
Imports:
    dplyr,
    ggdist,
    rlang,
    ggplot2,
    patchwork
Suggests:
    testthat (>= 3.0.0)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.1.1
